cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project, please cite it as below — and please also cite the referenced literature."
title: "wuxing-math: 五行数学之旅 — A mathematical journey of the Chinese Five Elements (Wu Xing), from the 5-cycle / affine Cartan matrix A4(1) to fold phase transitions"
abstract: >-
  An independent, exploratory mathematical reconstruction of the Chinese Five-Elements
  (Wu Xing) system. It encodes the five elements as a 5-cycle whose generative relation
  is a cyclic permutation matrix R with R^5 = I (a 5th-order cyclic group of orthogonal
  matrices), identifies the Wu-Xing graph with the affine Dynkin diagram A4(1) and its
  generalized Cartan matrix A = 2I - Adj(C5) (positive semidefinite, corank 1, with the
  golden ratio appearing in its nonzero spectrum), studies the generation/restriction
  couplings as positive/negative feedback in a self-stabilizing network (with a phase
  diagram whose critical boundary is a + b = 1), and shows that a nonlinear over-restraint
  ("cheng/wu") term yields a fold (saddle-node) phase transition with bistability and
  hysteresis.
